course: dictionary
lesson: 13048
title: Fastened: closed or fixed firmly
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Fastened is the past tense of fasten. It means closed or joined firmly, so that it will not come open. «Please make sure your seatbelt is fastened before the car moves.» A seatbelt that is fastened is done up and held tight.
explain: Fastened can also mean fixed firmly to something. «The picture was fastened to the wall with two pins.» The pins hold the picture in place, so it stays still. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Try closed, fixed or done up in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Look for clues around the word. «The gate was fastened shut with a chain.» Shut and chain tell you the gate was locked closed. Some words have more than one meaning, so the words around them show which meaning the author means.
fact: Fasten is a verb. Fastened is its past tense, and it can also be used as an adjective.
fact: «Fastened» means closed or joined firmly, like a button that is done up.
fact: «Fastened» also means fixed firmly to something, like a picture fastened to a wall.
fact: «Fastened on» can mean that your eyes or attention are fixed on something.
fact: «Keep your seatbelt fastened» means keep it done up while you travel.
exercise: «Please keep your seatbelt fastened until the plane has landed.» What does fastened mean here? | *Done up and closed firmly | Painted bright red | Thrown away | Loose and open
exercise: «The little boy fastened his coat before he went out into the snow.» What did the boy do to his coat? | Left it on the bus | Tore it in two | *Did it up | Took it off
exercise: «The gate was fastened shut with a chain.» Find and copy the word that means closed firmly. | chain | *fastened | gate | with
test: «The picture was fastened to the wall with two pins.» What does fastened mean? | Painted over | Hidden under a blanket | Taken down and thrown away | *Fixed firmly to something
test: Ella says, «My helmet must be fastened before I ride my bike.» What does Ella mean? | The helmet is new | Ella has lost the helmet | *Its straps are done up and secure | The helmet is too big to wear
exam: «Mia's eyes were fastened on the screen.» What does fastened on mean here? | *Her eyes were fixed on the screen | She was too tired to look | She ran away from the screen | Her eyes were shut tight
